    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP today, the offensive strategy is heavily weighted toward capitalizing on favorable matchups against suspect pitching. **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 79.27 score; while facing a lefty typically dampens his outlook, the high 5.41 xERA of Aldegheri makes him a must-start, providing a massive ceiling for speed and run production. Joining him at the top of the board is **Jose Caballero** (74.03), who benefits from a sharp +13% platoon boost against Kay, and **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90), whose ability to exploit Sullivan\u2019s 4.99 xERA makes him an essential anchor in the outfield. **James Wood** also remains a focal point; with an xwOBA of .407 and an elite 72.03 score, he is positioned to capitalize on his leadoff spot against Avila, mitigating the slight speed-reduction penalty from the opposing battery.\n\nRegarding our bench decisions, **Cole Young** was the closest to cracking the lineup with a 40.07 score, but ultimately lacked the high-ceiling matchup profile required to supplant our current starters. The optimizer favored the aggressive platoon matchups of **Travis Bazzana** and **Kyle Karros** despite their lower floors, prioritizing the exploitability of their respective matchups over **Cole Young**'s neutral outlook against Bradish. We are closely monitoring the lineup stability for **Alex Freeland**, who sits at a marginal 42.49 score; his position at the bottom of the order against a tough arm in McClanahan provides the lowest floor in our active lineup. While we remain thin at the corner spots with **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Josh Naylor** sidelined, the current group is well-positioned to drive SB totals while navigating the park factors that elevated **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Austin Riley** into strong starting territory today.",
